# Force LF on files consumed by the Linux container, regardless of a
# developer's core.autocrlf setting on Windows. Without this, a Windows
# checkout rewrites entrypoint.sh to CRLF and the container crash-loops with:
#   exec /entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
# (the shebang becomes "#!/bin/sh\r", so Linux looks for an interpreter
# literally named /bin/sh\r). Added by the fork; upstream ships none.
*.sh           text eol=lf
*.conf         text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh  text eol=lf
Dockerfile     text eol=lf
